      <floats-group id="article-31341.s8">
        <fig id="article-31341.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Key&#x000a0;Principles of the Western Blot Procedure. This image depicts 3 key principles of&#x000a0;the Western blot process. First, electrophoresis separates proteins using a discontinuous buffer system. Next, proteins are transferred from the gel onto a membrane using a wet-transfer sandwich. Finally, the membrane is probed with primary and secondary antibodies to detect specific target proteins. Contributed by Kartheek Gavini, MS</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="WBmsfinal" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
